Original change's description:
> Reland "[ganesh] Guard GrBufferAllocPool against overflow"
>
> This is a reland of commit 774ce6985eb2eed8b822f8045edabc9d698eeeba
>
> Original change's description:
> > [ganesh] Guard GrBufferAllocPool against overflow
> >
> > Previously, GrBufferAllocPool::makeSpaceAtLeast checked whether the
> > active block had sufficient space using raw unsigned addition (minSize +
> > pad), which could wrap around size_t when minSize was near SIZE_MAX and
> > write padding out of bounds.
> >
> > Check alignment rounding, padding additions, and vertex/index/indirect
> > byte multiplications with SkSafeMath, and reject zero or negative sizes
> > and counts. Cap single-block allocations to 1.5 GiB, make
> > GrCpuBuffer::Make fallible via sk_malloc_canfail so oversized or OOM
> > allocations return nullptr and skip the draw, and cap
> > GrVertexChunkBuilder's initial heuristic preallocation to 512 KiB
> > (growing up to 16 MiB per chunk as vertices are written) with a fallback
> > to the default buffer size.
> >
